Z||000010||stimpy||11-26-2000||10:46 PM||||I've cot a total of about 8 hours of work on my left arm (Alien Bhudda meditating under a Yin-Yang, was in Skin-Art magazine, all color) and about 4 hours black work on my right arm (nothing terribly artistic, kinda just punk rock bullsh!t). Tattoos are terribly addicting. So now I live in a state where it illegal to tattoo. <P>As far as the raised outline, I think it has more to do with the dep of the needle when the work is getting done.  Of course some scabbing will occur with any tattoo, but if it is kept moist during the healing with neosporin, then it shouldn't leach too much color out. the most important thing is to keep it out of the sun, and not have anything rub on it while it heals.||||reg||1
